==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|erthely}}, {{m|enm|erthlich}}, {{m|enm|ierðlich}}, from {{inh|en|ang|eorþlīċ}}, corresponding to {{suf|en|earth|ly|id2=adjectival}}. Cognate with {{cog|non|jarðligr|t=earthly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈəːθli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-earthly.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|earthlier}}

# Relating to the [[earth]] or this world, as opposed to heaven; [[terrestrial]].
#: '''''earthly''' joys''
#* {{RQ:Milton WFAL|passage=This '''earthly''' load / Of death, called life.}}
#* {{rfdatek|en|Bible}}, Phil. iii. 19
#*: whose glory is in their shame, who mind '''earthly''' things
# {{lb|en|negative|informal}} {{non-gloss definition|Used for emphasis}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Made of earth; [[earthy]].
#: {{rfquotek|en|Holland}}

